 "text": "9/29/26, 9:42 AM\nchange in period demand only influences the forecast period that follows directly after.\n\nThe expected meter reading is determined as follows:\n\n1. Determination of meter reading difference 01-2 to 01-1: 1,200 kWh 1,000 kWh = 200 kWh\n=> Consumption for 01-2 = 200 kWh\n\n2. Determination of consumption per weighting unit: 200 kWh : 300 = 2/3 kWh\n\n3. Extrapolation of consumption for period 01-4 to 01-5: 2/3 kWh300 = 200 kWh\n=> Meter reading difference for period 01-4 to 01-5= 200 kWh\n\n4. Determination of the expected meter reading to 01-5 by adding the meter reading difference to meter reading 01-4:\n2,000 kWh + 200 kWh = 2,200 kWh\n\nThe expected meter reading at time 01-5 is 2,200 kWh.\n\nee Example\n\nExample 7: Forecasts from period of the previous year and changes to period consumption in the previous year but not in\n\nthe base period\n|---| \u2014\u2014_\u2014_\u2014_}--\u2014-----|--------- | \u2014\u2014\u2014_}-\n1.1.96 4.1.96                   12.31.96 3.30.97\n\nMR Result       1,000             1,200              2,000           ?kWh\n\nomen e|] $$] |--\u2014---\u2014--- |_\u2014___|--\nMR Reas.         P,                 P,       P3       Py              P5\n\n01-1                01-2      01-3      01-4             01-5\n1,000                                          1,2                            kWh/Year\nPer. Cons. |\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014_\u2014\u2014__\n1.11.96\n\nWoght. Units                  150          150                                                300\n\nee |------\u2014\u2014- SOanIRRIEEnnniaanal mnimmappeetaam|---\nWght. Por.            15%    15%                          30%\n\nOn 1.1.96 a period consumption value of 1,000 kWh / year was entered for the register. On 11.1.96 for the period 01-2 to 01-3,\nthis value was changed to 1,200 kWh / year.\n\nThe minimum portion of weighting in percent is 30%.\nThe sum of the weighting units for one year is 1,000.\n\nWith a weighting portion of 30%, period 01-2 to 01-1 from the previous year is representative. No changed were made to the\nperiod consumption within this period. The changes that were made to the period cosnumption between 01-2 and 01-3 do not\n",
